 "text": "Hi, how you doing? Sure. It' a color made by adding pure pigment to a clear base like oil. Complementary means opposite, and these pairs contrast beautifully. It gives strong, vibrant colors that hold up well under different lighting. contrast makes them pop. That's one way to do it, yes. Black is strong and can make colors look dull. Then use it for details that need sharpness. Stick to pure pigment for shadows. It stays color true without getting weak.",
